---
description: Compact conversation, files, and logs into a verified CONTEXT-COMPACT.md at 70% of declared max context.
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `context-compactor`:

1. Declare your max context at session start. At 70% estimated usage — or before a task switch, new chat, or handoff — compact before continuing.
2. Write the state to `CONTEXT-COMPACT.md` in the project root (gitignored): goal, decisions verbatim, open tasks, next step, file map, user corrections verbatim, errors and evidence, session state.
3. Never summarize away IDs, hashes, paths, numbers, dates, exact error messages, or the user's own wording for decisions and corrections.
4. Crush long logs with the script instead of loading them whole, and verify the compact with the script's `check` (all sections present, every must-keep fact present verbatim) before dropping the raw history.

Read `~/.cursor/skills/context-compactor/SKILL.md` (or `.cursor/skills/context-compactor/SKILL.md`).
